--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -3,3 +3,14 @@
 A small TypeScript library, with no runtime dependency, of building blocks for our services that store,
 exchange and update JSON: configuration files, API payloads and stored records. It is imported by the
 other projects of the team, so its behaviour must follow the published standards it implements.
+
+## JSON Pointer (RFC 6901)
+
+`resolvePointer(document, pointer)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, returns the value of `document`
+that `pointer` refers to. The empty pointer is the whole document. It throws an `Error` when the
+pointer is not valid (no leading `/`, or a `~` not followed by `0` or `1`) or does not resolve: missing
+member, array index out of range or not canonical (`01`, `+1`), the `-` token, or a step into a
+primitive. Only own members are resolved, so `/__proto__` and `/length` do not resolve. The URI
+fragment form (`#/a`) is not supported.
+
+Run the tests with `npm test` (Node 22.18 or later, which runs TypeScript directly).
